+# Homepage paint monitoring
+
+`scripts/performance-monitor.js` observes navigation links, Order Now, and Seasonal
+Favorites cards (including their detail links) without intercepting clicks or
+changing destinations. It also observes browser-detected client-side soft
+navigations, including routes whose content paints before their URL changes.
+The current homepage has ordinary document links and no client-side router.
+This instrumentation does not convert those links to client-side navigation or
+measure the destination document's load from the departing homepage.
+
+Measurements are available from `window.dailyGrindPerformance.getRecords()`
+(the latest 100 reports) and the `daily-grind:performance` window event:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => {
+  // Forward detail to your existing analytics system here.
+});
+```
+
+No data is sent over the network automatically. Reports contain stable control
+labels and destination pathnames rather than query strings, DOM references, or
+account content. `window.dailyGrindPerformance.capabilities` describes the
+observers successfully registered in the current browser.
+
+- `interaction-contentful-paint`: `duration` is milliseconds from the initiating
+  interaction to contentful paint presentation, including attributed async work.
+  Successively larger painted content produces updated candidates for the same
+  `interactionId`; these are updates, not separate clicks. A paint is not a
+  guarantee that every animation or background task has finished.
+- `soft-navigation`: `fcpDuration` and `lcpDuration` measure the route's first and
+  latest largest contentful paint relative to its initiating interaction. The
+  report is finalized on the next soft navigation, visibility becoming hidden,
+  pagehide, or an explicit `window.dailyGrindPerformance.flush()` call.
+- `interaction-next-paint`: Event Timing's input-to-next-frame duration for
+  tracked clicks. This is a separate responsiveness metric, **not** completion
+  of asynchronously loaded content. Its minimum reporting threshold is 16 ms,
+  with browser rounding; faster clicks may not produce entries.
+
+The contentful-paint and soft-navigation APIs have limited browser availability.
+Unsupported observers are skipped; Event Timing remains available independently
+where supported. No timer-based estimate is presented as actual paint timing.
+Clicks with no attributed contentful update do not generate contentful reports.
+
+Run non-browser checks with:
+
+```sh
+node --check scripts/performance-monitor.js
+node --test scripts/performance-monitor.test.cjs
+```
